<Project>
  <PropertyGroup>
    <Nullable>enable</Nullable>
    <ImplicitUsings>enable</ImplicitUsings>
    <TreatWarningsAsErrors>true</TreatWarningsAsErrors>
    <LangVersion>latest</LangVersion>
    <ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>true</ManagePackageVersionsCentrally>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- Shared package identity for all packable projects (core + dialect satellites).
       Inert for non-packable projects (tests, benchmarks). -->
  <PropertyGroup Label="Packaging">
    <Version>1.11.2</Version>
    <PackageReleaseNotes>
New: x.SqlParam() and x.SqlIdentifier() -- the two doors a raw string can take into SQL, now discoverable in IntelliSense with no extra using. Sql.Text is deprecated in favour of x.SqlParam() (warning; removed in 2.0). Sql.Identifier is unchanged.

Fixes: ToDebug() on SQL Server emitted DECLARE @@p001_x -- a doubled @, which is T-SQL's system-variable prefix, so the script was invalid and could not be pasted into SSMS. Parameter names could contain characters SQL rejects (Sql.Text("literal") produced @p001_"literal"). Parameter scopes are now 1-based, so the first command emits @p001_* as the docs have always said -- it was emitting @p000_*.

NOTE: generated parameter NAMES change in this release. They are not API, but if you hardcoded one in AppendRaw or snapshot-tested generated SQL, you will see a diff.

Full notes: https://github.com/purelogictek-inc/DapperPipeline/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md
    </PackageReleaseNotes>
    <Authors>PureLogicTek, Inc.</Authors>
    <Company>PureLogicTek, Inc.</Company>
    <Copyright>Copyright (c) 2026 PureLogicTek, Inc.</Copyright>
    <PackageLicenseExpression>MIT</PackageLicenseExpression>
    <PackageReadmeFile>README.md</PackageReadmeFile>
    <PackageProjectUrl>https://github.com/purelogictek-inc/DapperPipeline</PackageProjectUrl>
    <RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/purelogictek-inc/DapperPipeline</RepositoryUrl>
    <RepositoryType>git</RepositoryType>
    <PublishRepositoryUrl>true</PublishRepositoryUrl>
    <IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
    <SymbolPackageFormat>snupkg</SymbolPackageFormat>
    <PackageIcon>icon.png</PackageIcon>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <ItemGroup Label="Packaging">
    <None Include="$(MSBuildThisFileDirectory)assets/icon.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" Visible="false" />
  </ItemGroup>
</Project>
